    {
      "id": "l9ebcwl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Metals are electropositive elements that lose electrons to form positive ions, characterized by metallic luster, malleability, and high electrical conductivity.",
        "Non-metals are electronegative elements that gain or share electrons, forming acidic or neutral oxides when reacted with oxygen.",
        "The Reactivity Series ranks metals in decreasing order of reactivity, with Potassium at the top and Gold at the bottom.",
        "Extraction methods depend on reactivity: highly reactive metals are extracted via electrolysis, while moderately reactive ones undergo reduction with carbon."
      ],
      "id": "rqcxqkw"
    },
