      "id": "1ij8m5j",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Extraction of Metals"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Sodium and Potassium are soft metals that can be cut with a knife and must be stored in kerosene to prevent reaction with moisture.",
        "Mercury is the only liquid metal at room temperature, whereas Bromine is the only liquid non-metal.",
        "Amphoteric oxides like Aluminium Oxide (Al2O3) and Zinc Oxide (ZnO) react with both acids and bases to produce salt and water.",
        "Aqua Regia (3:1 ratio of concentrated HCl and concentrated HNO3) can dissolve noble metals like Gold and Platinum."
      ],
      "id": "r31cgu0"
    },
